+/**
+ * struct hx_pen_path - state of the independent pen detector.
+ *
+ * The tunables live flat in struct hx_algo (pen_enabled, pen_threshold,
+ * pen_jump_max, pen_confirm_frames, pen_lost_frames) because that is what
+ * the HX_ALGO_ATTR_*_RW() macros address: they expand to ts->algo->_name.
+ * Only the state lives here.
+ *
+ * Why the path exists at all:
+ *
+ * The amplitude pipeline (phases 2A..2D) requires a candidate to clear
+ * macro_threshold to seed a zone and peak_threshold to become a peak.  That
+ * suits a fingertip -- 4x5 cells, peak ~3800 -- and cannot suit a conductive
+ * pen tip on this panel, which measures 2x2 cells, peak ~490, skirt 40..80,
+ * against a resting noise floor of sigma ~34 and max 120.  Replayed over the
+ * 2026-09-30 recording, dropping the pair to 60/150 makes the resting panel
+ * emit 0.59 contacts per frame against 1.22 while the pen was writing -- no
+ * separation at any setting, because amplitude alone cannot tell them apart.
+ *
+ * Shape in time can.  The recorded stroke advanced 1.4 cells per frame
+ * (median), worst case 4.2, for 313 consecutive frames inside one 7x8-cell
+ * patch.  Noise jumps at random.  Replayed over the same recording this path
+ * reported 313 of 424 pen frames, 0 with the panel at rest and 0 with the pen
+ * hovering 5 mm above it.
+ *
+ * @has, @last_r, @last_c: last accepted candidate
+ * @conf:        current streak length
+ * @miss:        consecutive frames without a candidate
+ * @active:      latched; a contact is emitted
+ * @x, @y:       last emitted position in Q8.8 grid coordinates
+ * @z:           raw-grid value at the last accepted candidate
+ * @frames_cand: frames with a candidate above pen_threshold
+ * @frames_emit: frames the path was latched and emitted
